(function () {
	let navigationId = 0;
	let pendingImage = null;

	function updateIllustration(event) {
		const passage = event.passage;
		const artTag = passage.tags.find(function (tag) {
			return tag.indexOf("art-") === 0;
		});
		const sceneArt = artTag && setup.sceneImages[artTag];
		const figure = document.getElementById("persistent-illustration");
		const image = document.getElementById("persistent-illustration-image");
		const targetUrl = sceneArt ? new URL(sceneArt.src, document.baseURI).href : null;

		if (!targetUrl) {
			navigationId += 1;
			pendingImage = null;
			figure.hidden = true;
			image.removeAttribute("data-image-url");
			return;
		}

		if (image.getAttribute("data-image-url") === targetUrl) {
			navigationId += 1;
			pendingImage = null;
			return;
		}

		if (pendingImage && pendingImage.url === targetUrl) {
			pendingImage.navigationId = ++navigationId;
			return;
		}

		const request = {
			url: targetUrl,
			navigationId: ++navigationId
		};
		const preload = new Image();
		pendingImage = request;

		preload.onload = function () {
			if (pendingImage !== request || request.navigationId !== navigationId) {
				return;
			}

			image.src = targetUrl;
			image.alt = sceneArt.alt;
			image.setAttribute("data-image-url", targetUrl);
			figure.hidden = false;
			pendingImage = null;
		};

		preload.onerror = function () {
			if (pendingImage !== request || request.navigationId !== navigationId) {
				return;
			}

			console.error("Could not load scene illustration: " + targetUrl);
			pendingImage = null;
		};

		preload.src = targetUrl;
	}

	$(document)
		.off(":passagedisplay.persistentIllustration")
		.on(":passagedisplay.persistentIllustration", updateIllustration);
})();

:: Opening [art-01]
<p class="narration">Rain tapped the window. The boy had a blanket, a glass of water and an impressive collection of toys arranged to make illness look productive.</p>
<p class="narration">His grandfather entered carrying a thick book.</p>
<p class="dialogue framing-dialogue"><span class="speaker">Grandson:</span> “Is that homework?”</p>
<p class="dialogue framing-dialogue"><span class="speaker">Grandfather:</span> “Worse. Literature.”</p>
<p class="dialogue framing-dialogue"><span class="speaker">Grandson:</span> “I knew you were up to something.”</p>
<p class="dialogue framing-dialogue"><span class="speaker">Grandfather:</span> “This one has sword fights, pirates, a giant and a prince who is very pleased with himself.”</p>
<p class="dialogue framing-dialogue"><span class="speaker">Grandson:</span> “Does the prince get punched?”</p>
<p class="dialogue framing-dialogue"><span class="speaker">Grandfather:</span> “You're asking excellent questions remarkably early.”</p>
<p>How does the boy negotiate the reading?</p>
<ul class="choices">
	<li><<link "“Start with the sword fights.”" "OpeningSword">><</link>></li>
	<li><<link "“No kissing.”" "OpeningNoKissing">><</link>></li>
	<li><<link "“Can I choose what happens?”" "OpeningChoice">><</link>></li>
</ul>

:: OpeningSword [art-01]
<p class="dialogue framing-dialogue"><span class="speaker">Grandfather:</span> “We must first meet the people holding the swords.”</p>
<p class="dialogue framing-dialogue"><span class="speaker">Grandson:</span> “Fine. But introduce them quickly.”</p>
<p class="continue"><<link "Continue reading." "OpeningRejoin">><</link>></p>

:: OpeningNoKissing [art-01]
<p class="dialogue framing-dialogue"><span class="speaker">Grandfather:</span> “I can offer a reasonable amount of sword fighting in exchange.”</p>
<p class="dialogue framing-dialogue"><span class="speaker">Grandson:</span> “That wasn't a yes.”</p>
<p class="dialogue framing-dialogue"><span class="speaker">Grandfather:</span> “You're learning to negotiate.”</p>
<p class="continue"><<link "Continue reading." "OpeningRejoin">><</link>></p>

:: OpeningChoice [art-01]
<p class="dialogue framing-dialogue"><span class="speaker">Grandfather:</span> “You may choose what people say and do. I reserve the right to keep the story from becoming nonsense.”</p>
<p class="dialogue framing-dialogue"><span class="speaker">Grandson:</span> “That sounds unfair.”</p>
<p class="dialogue framing-dialogue"><span class="speaker">Grandfather:</span> “Most authors would agree.”</p>
<p class="continue"><<link "Continue reading." "OpeningRejoin">><</link>></p>

:: OpeningRejoin [art-01]
<p class="narration">The grandfather opened the book. On the first page was a farm, which the boy regarded with immediate suspicion.</p>
<p class="continue"><<link "Turn to the first page." "FarmOpening">><</link>></p>

:: FarmOpening [art-02]
<p class="narration">The farm had a leaky roof, a temperamental horse and a gate that refused to close. Buttercup believed these problems could all be solved by Westley.</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Buttercup:</span> “The gate is broken again.”</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Westley:</span> “A tragedy. Shall I inform the king?”</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Buttercup:</span> “You could fix it.”</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Westley:</span> “An excellent alternative to bothering the king.”</p>
<p class="narration">He worked while she watched. She had recently developed the irritating habit of finding reasons to watch.</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Buttercup:</span> “You don't have to agree with everything I say.”</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Westley:</span> “I've been waiting for permission to disagree about the horse.”</p>
<p>Buttercup attempts to say what she actually means.</p>
<ul class="choices">
	<li><<link "“I like having you here.”" "FarmLike">><</link>></li>
	<li><<link "“That gate is crooked.”" "FarmGate">><</link>></li>
	<li><<link "“Perhaps you should stop agreeing with me.”" "FarmDisagree">><</link>></li>
</ul>

:: FarmLike [art-02]
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Westley:</span> “Even when I'm not repairing something?”</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Buttercup:</span> “Let's not get carried away.”</p>
<p class="narration">He smiles; she doesn't look away.</p>
<p class="continue"><<link "Continue." "FarmRejoin">><</link>></p>

:: FarmGate [art-02]
<p class="narration">Westley checks it with exaggerated care.</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Westley:</span> “Remarkable. It was straight until you came outside.”</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Buttercup:</span> “Are you blaming me?”</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Westley:</span> “Only the gate would dare.”</p>
<p class="continue"><<link "Continue." "FarmRejoin">><</link>></p>

:: FarmDisagree [art-02]
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Westley:</span> “I disagree.”</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Buttercup:</span> “You are impossible.”</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Westley:</span> “We finally agree.”</p>
<p class="continue"><<link "Continue." "FarmRejoin">><</link>></p>

:: FarmRejoin [art-02]
<p class="narration">Westley shut the repaired gate. Buttercup reached for the latch at the same time as he did. Neither moved their hand immediately.</p>
<p class="continue"><<link "Continue down the road." "HorizonOpening">><</link>></p>

:: HorizonOpening [art-03]
<p class="narration">Westley had decided to leave and earn enough money to return with a future worth offering. He had rehearsed a dignified farewell. The rehearsal had not included Buttercup looking at him like that.</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Buttercup:</span> “How long?”</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Westley:</span> “I don't know.”</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Buttercup:</span> “An ambitious answer.”</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Westley:</span> “I considered inventing a number. You would have noticed.”</p>
<p>What does Westley leave her with?</p>
<ul class="choices">
	<li><<link "A practical promise." "HorizonPromise">><</link>></li>
	<li><<link "A joke." "HorizonJoke">><</link>></li>
	<li><<link "A grand declaration." "HorizonDeclaration">><</link>></li>
</ul>

:: HorizonPromise [art-03]
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Westley:</span> “I'll write whenever I can.”</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Buttercup:</span> “Then I'll complain about your handwriting whenever you do.”</p>
<p class="narration">She squeezes his hand.</p>
<p class="continue"><<link "Continue." "HorizonRejoin">><</link>></p>

:: HorizonJoke [art-03]
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Westley:</span> “Please don't let the horse manage the farm. He has expensive tastes.”</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Buttercup:</span> “He'll miss you.”</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Westley:</span> “I was hoping someone would.”</p>
<p class="continue"><<link "Continue." "HorizonRejoin">><</link>></p>

:: HorizonDeclaration [art-03]
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Westley:</span> “Nothing in the world will keep me away forever.”</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Buttercup:</span> “You haven't seen much of the world.”</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Westley:</span> “Then it had better be on its best behaviour.”</p>
<p class="continue"><<link "Continue." "HorizonRejoin">><</link>></p>

:: HorizonRejoin [art-03]
<p class="narration">He walked down the road. Buttercup watched until she could no longer see him. Neither had said the most important thing plainly, but both had heard it.</p>
<p class="continue"><<link "Continue." "LetterOpening">><</link>></p>

:: LetterOpening [art-04]
<p class="narration">A messenger arrived with news of a ship attacked by pirates. Westley had been aboard. No survivors were known.</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Messenger:</span> “I'm sorry. I wish I had better news.”</p>
<p class="narration">Buttercup looked at the road beyond him.</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Buttercup:</span> “Do you know for certain?”</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Messenger:</span> “No.”</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Buttercup:</span> “Then don't ask me to be certain for you.”</p>
<p>What does she do next?</p>
<ul class="choices">
	<li><<link "Ask for every detail." "LetterDetails">><</link>></li>
	<li><<link "Close the door." "LetterDoor">><</link>></li>
	<li><<link "Return to the day's work." "LetterWork">><</link>></li>
</ul>

:: LetterDetails [art-04]
<p class="narration">The messenger tells her what little he knows. She listens carefully, as if careful listening could bring him home.</p>
<p class="continue"><<link "Continue." "LetterRejoin">><</link>></p>

:: LetterDoor [art-04]
<p class="narration">She shuts out the messenger, but not his words. After a long while she opens the door again. He has gone.</p>
<p class="continue"><<link "Continue." "LetterRejoin">><</link>></p>

:: LetterWork [art-04]
<p class="narration">She carries a bucket to the gate, sets it down, and cannot remember why she picked it up.</p>
<p class="continue"><<link "Continue." "LetterRejoin">><</link>></p>

:: LetterRejoin [art-04]
<p class="narration">Westley's gate still closed perfectly. Buttercup hated it for that, then hated herself for hating it. Seasons passed.</p>
<p class="continue"><<link "Continue to the palace." "ProposalOpening">><</link>></p>

:: ProposalOpening
<p class="narration">Prince Humperdinck had a talent for turning a conversation into an announcement.</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Humperdinck:</span> “Our marriage will delight the kingdom.”</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Buttercup:</span> “Has the kingdom been consulted?”</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Humperdinck:</span> “It will be delighted. I have arranged it.”</p>
<p class="narration">He gestured towards a row of gardeners, all suddenly working with unnatural enthusiasm.</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Humperdinck:</span> “You will have jewels, gowns, guards and whatever else a princess requires.”</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Buttercup:</span> “A choice?”</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Humperdinck:</span> “Within reason.”</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Buttercup:</span> “And who decides what's reasonable?”</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Humperdinck:</span> “I admire your interest in government.”</p>
<p>Buttercup tests the prince's sincerity.</p>
<ul class="choices">
	<li><<link "“What if I don't love you?”" "ProposalLove">><</link>></li>
	<li><<link "“What exactly would you expect?”" "ProposalExpectations">><</link>></li>
	<li><<link "“I need time to think.”" "ProposalTime">><</link>></li>
</ul>

:: ProposalLove
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Humperdinck:</span> “People adore the royal family without knowing us personally.”</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Buttercup:</span> “That explains a great deal.”</p>
<p class="continue"><<link "Continue." "ProposalRejoin">><</link>></p>

:: ProposalExpectations
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Humperdinck:</span> “Attend ceremonies. Smile. Avoid surprises.”</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Buttercup:</span> “I can promise to attend.”</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Humperdinck:</span> “Splendid.”</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Buttercup:</span> “I said nothing about the other two.”</p>
<p class="continue"><<link "Continue." "ProposalRejoin">><</link>></p>

:: ProposalTime
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Humperdinck:</span> “Take the afternoon.”</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Buttercup:</span> “Generous.”</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Humperdinck:</span> “I'm known for it.”</p>
<p class="continue"><<link "Continue." "ProposalRejoin">><</link>></p>

:: ProposalRejoin
<p class="narration">Buttercup accepted a future she did not want, convinced that the one she did want had disappeared at sea. The palace began ordering flowers by the cartload.</p>
<p class="continue"><<link "Continue." "KidnappingOpening">><</link>></p>

:: KidnappingOpening [art-05]
<p class="narration">The kidnapping was efficient only if you ignored the shouting. A small man issued commands, a giant lifted Buttercup with surprising gentleness, and a swordsman apologised twice before they reached the boat.</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Vizzini:</span> “A flawless operation!”</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Vizzini:</span> “We're kidnappers!”</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Fezzik:</span> “It's windy.”</p>
<p>Whom does Buttercup question?</p>
<ul class="choices">
	<li><<link "Fezzik: “Are you always this polite?”" "KidnapFezzik">><</link>></li>
	<li><<link "Iñigo: “You don't seem proud of this work.”" "KidnapInigo">><</link>></li>
	<li><<link "Vizzini: “What happens if your plan fails?”" "KidnapVizzini">><</link>></li>
</ul>

:: KidnapFezzik [art-05]
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Fezzik:</span> “Not when I'm asleep.”</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Buttercup:</span> “Fair enough.”</p>
<p class="narration">He offers the blanket anyway.</p>
<p class="continue"><<link "Continue." "KidnappingRejoin">><</link>></p>

:: KidnapInigo [art-05]
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Iñigo:</span> “I have performed better work. Some of it involved less shouting.”</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Vizzini:</span> “I HEARD THAT!”</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Iñigo:</span> “That is what I mean.”</p>
<p class="continue"><<link "Continue." "KidnappingRejoin">><</link>></p>

:: KidnapVizzini [art-05]
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Vizzini:</span> “Then I shall demonstrate why failure was the cleverest possible outcome.”</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Buttercup:</span> “How convenient.”</p>
<p class="continue"><<link "Continue." "KidnappingRejoin">><</link>></p>

:: KidnappingRejoin [art-05]
<p class="narration">A black sail appeared behind them.</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Fezzik:</span> “Someone is following us.”</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Vizzini:</span> “Impossible. I planned not to be followed.”</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Buttercup:</span> “Perhaps they didn't receive the plan.”</p>
<p class="narration">Vizzini ordered the boat towards the Cliffs of Insanity. His crew exchanged the sort of look that suggested they had already regretted several career decisions.</p>
<p class="continue"><<link "Continue to the cliffs." "CliffsOpening">><</link>></p>

:: CliffsOpening [art-06]
<p class="narration">The stranger in black climbed the last stretch of rock. Iñigo waited at the top with his sword sheathed.</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Stranger:</span> “Are you going to attack me?”</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Iñigo:</span> “Eventually. It seems rude to interrupt a man who has just climbed a cliff.”</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Stranger:</span> “You have an unusual sense of hospitality.”</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Iñigo:</span> “I was raised properly. I also intend to win.”</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Stranger:</span> “A host with modest ambitions.”</p>
<p>How does Iñigo open the conversation?</p>
<ul class="choices">
	<li><<link "“Who taught you the sword?”" "CliffsTeacher">><</link>></li>
	<li><<link "“Would you like to surrender?”" "CliffsSurrender">><</link>></li>
	<li><<link "“I have trained for twenty years.”" "CliffsTraining">><</link>></li>
</ul>

:: CliffsTeacher [art-06]
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Stranger:</span> “Several men. Some were better teachers after I stopped listening.”</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Iñigo:</span> “A familiar educational method.”</p>
<p class="continue"><<link "Draw your swords." "DuelOpening">><</link>></p>

:: CliffsSurrender [art-06]
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Stranger:</span> “Would you?”</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Iñigo:</span> “No.”</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Stranger:</span> “Then we have saved ourselves two speeches.”</p>
<p class="continue"><<link "Draw your swords." "DuelOpening">><</link>></p>

:: CliffsTraining [art-06]
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Stranger:</span> “Excellent. I had hoped not to spend the afternoon instructing a beginner.”</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Iñigo:</span> “I am beginning to dislike you.”</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Stranger:</span> “That usually happens after the duel.”</p>
<p class="continue"><<link "Draw your swords." "DuelOpening">><</link>></p>

:: DuelOpening [art-07]
<p class="narration">They drew their swords. Steel rang against steel. Iñigo stepped forward; the stranger gave ground, then stole it back. Their blades moved faster than their conversation, which annoyed them both.</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Iñigo:</span> “You are very good.”</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Stranger:</span> “Thank you. You are making it difficult to be smug.”</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Iñigo:</span> “I can slow down if you need time.”</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Stranger:</span> “Please don't. I'd hate to become overconfident.”</p>
<p>Iñigo tries a new tactic.</p>
<ul class="choices">
	<li><<link "Attempt a flamboyant flourish." "DuelFlourish">><</link>></li>
	<li><<link "Fight in absolute silence." "DuelSilence">><</link>></li>
	<li><<link "Offer a critique of the stranger's stance." "DuelCritique">><</link>></li>
</ul>

:: DuelFlourish [art-07]
<p class="narration">The stranger watches the elaborate movement.</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Stranger:</span> “Beautiful. Does it come with music?”</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Iñigo:</span> “Only if you survive the next part.”</p>
<p class="narration">They exchange a rapid series of blows.</p>
<p class="continue"><<link "Continue the duel." "DuelOutcome">><</link>></p>

:: DuelSilence [art-07]
<p class="narration">After several tense exchanges, the stranger says, “Are we sulking now? I wasn't informed.” Iñigo almost laughs, which costs him a step.</p>
<p class="continue"><<link "Continue the duel." "DuelOutcome">><</link>></p>

:: DuelCritique [art-07]
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Iñigo:</span> “Your left foot is too far back.”</p>
<p class="narration">The stranger adjusts and immediately gains ground.</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Stranger:</span> “Much better. I appreciate the lesson.”</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Iñigo:</span> “I regret the lesson.”</p>
<p class="continue"><<link "Continue the duel." "DuelOutcome">><</link>></p>

:: DuelOutcome [art-07]
<p class="narration">The stranger's blade found Iñigo's guard and knocked the sword from his hand. Iñigo stood unarmed at the cliff edge.</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Iñigo:</span> “You could finish this.”</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Stranger:</span> “I could. But then who would tell people how impressive I was?”</p>
<p class="narration">He stepped away, leaving Iñigo alive.</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Iñigo:</span> “I would have described you as insufferable.”</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Stranger:</span> “I'll settle for accurate.”</p>
<p class="dialogue framing-dialogue"><span class="speaker">Grandson:</span> “Wait, he lets him live? After all that fighting?”</p>
<p class="dialogue framing-dialogue"><span class="speaker">Grandfather:</span> “Some men can win a duel without insisting on winning an argument with a corpse.”</p>
<p class="dialogue framing-dialogue"><span class="speaker">Grandson:</span> “That was a strange sentence.”</p>
<p class="dialogue framing-dialogue"><span class="speaker">Grandfather:</span> “It's a strange story.”</p>
<p class="narration">The stranger hurried after the kidnappers. Iñigo recovered his sword, his pride, and a useful new respect for men in black.</p>
<p class="continue"><<link "Continue." "GiantOpening">><</link>></p>

:: GiantOpening [art-06]
<p class="narration">Fezzik stood across the path, broad enough to block it without trying.</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Fezzik:</span> “I have to stop you.”</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Westley:</span> “You sound disappointed.”</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Fezzik:</span> “I don't like hurting people.”</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Westley:</span> “Neither do I. This is already the nicest ambush I've had.”</p>
<p>How does Westley handle the giant?</p>
<ul class="choices">
	<li><<link "“Perhaps we could discuss a compromise.”" "GiantCompromise">><</link>></li>
	<li><<link "“You are enormous. Is that an advantage?”" "GiantSize">><</link>></li>
	<li><<link "“I surrender.”" "GiantSurrender">><</link>></li>
</ul>

:: GiantCompromise [art-06]
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Fezzik:</span> “Vizzini says compromises are for people who lose.”</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Westley:</span> “Does he say that often?”</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Fezzik:</span> “Usually when he's losing.”</p>
<p class="continue"><<link "Continue." "GiantFight">><</link>></p>

:: GiantSize [art-06]
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Fezzik:</span> “Sometimes I bump my head.”</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Westley:</span> “An unexpected weakness. I'll make a note.”</p>
<p class="continue"><<link "Continue." "GiantFight">><</link>></p>

:: GiantSurrender [art-06]
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Fezzik:</span> “Oh. That's a relief.”</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Westley:</span> “I meant I surrender the opportunity to be crushed. I'm still going through.”</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Fezzik:</span> “That's a very confusing surrender.”</p>
<p class="continue"><<link "Continue." "GiantFight">><</link>></p>

:: GiantFight [art-06]
<p class="narration">They grappled. Fezzik was stronger, Westley faster. At last the giant fell unconscious, more gently than a man of his size ought to have been able to fall.</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Westley:</span> “I hope he wakes with a good opinion of me.”</p>
<p class="narration">Ahead, Vizzini waited with Buttercup, a small table and two cups.</p>
<p class="continue"><<link "Face the genius." "WitsOpening">><</link>></p>

:: WitsOpening [art-08]
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Vizzini:</span> “At last! A contest worthy of my intellect.”</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Westley:</span> “I was expecting a rescue. I seem to have arrived at a lecture.”</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Vizzini:</span> “One of these cups is dangerous. You must reason your way to the safe one.”</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Buttercup:</span> “Does he know which is which?”</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Westley:</span> “I was about to ask.”</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Vizzini:</span> “Of course I know. I have deduced it.”</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Westley:</span> “From what?”</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Vizzini:</span> “From the fact that I am clever.”</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Buttercup:</span> “A surprisingly economical investigation.”</p>
<p>How does Westley challenge Vizzini's reasoning?</p>
<ul class="choices">
	<li><<link "“Explain your deduction from the beginning.”" "WitsChildhood">><</link>></li>
	<li><<link "“What if I switch the cups?”" "WitsSwitch">><</link>></li>
	<li><<link "“I refuse to participate in a contest without written rules.”" "WitsRules">><</link>></li>
</ul>

:: WitsChildhood [art-08]
<p class="narration">Vizzini begins with his childhood, moves on to the history of cups, and arrives at a lengthy complaint about teachers.</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Westley:</span> “We've established you're upset with education. Can we return to the drinks?”</p>
<p class="continue"><<link "Continue." "WitsSecondChoice">><</link>></p>

:: WitsSwitch [art-08]
<p class="narration">Vizzini snatches both cups away.</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Vizzini:</span> “You cannot outwit me with a trick I have already anticipated!”</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Westley:</span> “Then why did you move them?”</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Vizzini:</span> “To demonstrate my anticipation.”</p>
<p class="continue"><<link "Continue." "WitsSecondChoice">><</link>></p>

:: WitsRules [art-08]
<p class="narration">Vizzini demands paper. There is none. He attempts to write rules on the table with a twig.</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Buttercup:</span> “You appear to be losing to stationery.”</p>
<p class="continue"><<link "Continue." "WitsSecondChoice">><</link>></p>

:: WitsSecondChoice [art-08]
<p class="narration">Vizzini put the cups down with exaggerated care.</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Vizzini:</span> “Now choose.”</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Westley:</span> “You first.”</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Vizzini:</span> “I cannot. That would reveal my strategy.”</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Westley:</span> “You have a strategy?”</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Vizzini:</span> “Several. They contradict one another to confuse the enemy.”</p>
<p>What does Westley say next?</p>
<ul class="choices">
	<li><<link "“Then choose the cup you believe I want.”" "WitsReverse">><</link>></li>
	<li><<link "“Your safest option is to refuse both.”" "WitsRefuse">><</link>></li>
	<li><<link "“Let's ask Buttercup to judge.”" "WitsJudge">><</link>></li>
</ul>

:: WitsReverse [art-08]
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Vizzini:</span> “A simple reverse-psychology trap. Unless you know that I know, in which case—”</p>
<p class="narration">He stops, offended by his own sentence.</p>
<p class="continue"><<link "See how the contest ends." "WitsRejoin">><</link>></p>

:: WitsRefuse [art-08]
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Vizzini:</span> “I refuse to be told what I refuse!”</p>
<p class="narration">He takes a cup merely to prove his independence.</p>
<p class="continue"><<link "See how the contest ends." "WitsRejoin">><</link>></p>

:: WitsJudge [art-08]
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Buttercup:</span> “My judgement is that neither of you should be trusted with refreshments.”</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Vizzini:</span> “A biased tribunal!”</p>
<p class="continue"><<link "See how the contest ends." "WitsRejoin">><</link>></p>

:: WitsRejoin [art-08]
<p class="narration">Vizzini made his decision with a triumphant smile. Moments later, the smile deserted him. His cleverness had not protected him from the trap.</p>
<p class="dialogue framing-dialogue"><span class="speaker">Grandson:</span> “Was that really a battle of wits?”</p>
<p class="dialogue framing-dialogue"><span class="speaker">Grandfather:</span> “It was certainly a battle. Only one participant brought any wits.”</p>
<p class="dialogue framing-dialogue"><span class="speaker">Grandson:</span> “Buttercup?”</p>
<p class="dialogue framing-dialogue"><span class="speaker">Grandfather:</span> “An excellent answer.”</p>
<p class="narration">Buttercup was free, though she had no reason yet to trust the masked man who had rescued her.</p>
<p class="continue"><<link "Continue across the hills." "FaceMaskOpening">><</link>></p>

:: FaceMaskOpening [art-09]
<p class="narration">The masked stranger led Buttercup away from the clearing. He spoke carelessly of Westley, as though a man lost at sea could be dismissed with a shrug.</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Buttercup:</span> “You know nothing about him.”</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Stranger:</span> “Perhaps less than you think.”</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Buttercup:</span> “Then stop speaking as if you do.”</p>
<p class="narration">They stumbled on the slope. His mask came loose.</p>
<p class="narration">Westley.</p>
<p class="narration">Buttercup stared. He looked older and tired, but it was him.</p>
<p>What are her first words?</p>
<ul class="choices">
	<li><<link "“I thought you were dead.”" "FaceMaskDead">><</link>></li>
	<li><<link "“You let me argue with you!”" "FaceMaskArgue">><</link>></li>
	<li><<link "“Please tell me I'm not imagining this.”" "FaceMaskImagine">><</link>></li>
</ul>

:: FaceMaskDead [art-09]
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Westley:</span> “I know.”</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Buttercup:</span> “That was a dreadful thing to let me believe.”</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Westley:</span> “Yes. I'm sorry.”</p>
<p class="continue"><<link "Continue." "FaceMaskRejoin">><</link>></p>

:: FaceMaskArgue [art-09]
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Westley:</span> “You were winning.”</p>
<p class="narration">She tried to stay angry, then reached for him.</p>
<p class="continue"><<link "Continue." "FaceMaskRejoin">><</link>></p>

:: FaceMaskImagine [art-09]
<p class="narration">He took her hand.</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Westley:</span> “You're not.”</p>
<p class="narration">For once, he had nothing clever to add.</p>
<p class="continue"><<link "Continue." "FaceMaskRejoin">><</link>></p>

:: FaceMaskRejoin [art-09]
<p class="narration">They held each other. The reunion was real. So were the distant riders gathering on the hills behind them.</p>
<p class="continue"><<link "Enter the Fire Swamp." "SwampOpening">><</link>></p>

:: SwampOpening [art-10]
<p class="narration">The swamp had a poor reputation, which Westley began to think was generous. The ground steamed. Something large moved under the reeds.</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Buttercup:</span> “Is there a safer route?”</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Westley:</span> “Almost certainly.”</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Buttercup:</span> “Why aren't we taking it?”</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Westley:</span> “I haven't found it.”</p>
<p class="narration">Flames burst from the earth a few steps ahead.</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Buttercup:</span> “That seems like useful information.”</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Westley:</span> “We should put up a sign.”</p>
<p>How do they proceed?</p>
<ul class="choices">
	<li><<link "Follow the firm stones." "SwampStones">><</link>></li>
	<li><<link "Cut through the reeds." "SwampReeds">><</link>></li>
	<li><<link "Climb a fallen tree to scout." "SwampScout">><</link>></li>
</ul>

:: SwampStones [art-10]
<p class="narration">They pick their way slowly between vents.</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Buttercup:</span> “You could have suggested this earlier.”</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Westley:</span> “I was gathering evidence against the other routes.”</p>
<p class="continue"><<link "Continue through the swamp." "SwampCapture">><</link>></p>

:: SwampReeds [art-11]
<p class="narration">Something huge splashes towards them. They retreat at speed.</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Buttercup:</span> “Evidence gathered?”</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Westley:</span> “Convincingly.”</p>
<p class="dialogue framing-dialogue"><span class="speaker">Grandson:</span> “Why would anyone go into the reeds after hearing a monster?”</p>
<p class="dialogue framing-dialogue"><span class="speaker">Grandfather:</span> “Some people insist on testing a warning personally.”</p>
<p class="dialogue framing-dialogue"><span class="speaker">Grandson:</span> “That's what the sign was for!”</p>
<p class="dialogue framing-dialogue"><span class="speaker">Grandfather:</span> “An excellent point. Shall I send the author a letter?”</p>
<p class="continue"><<link "Try another route." "SwampOpening">><</link>></p>

:: SwampScout [art-10]
<p class="narration">Westley spots a narrow passage.</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Buttercup:</span> “And the riders?”</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Westley:</span> “Also spotted. They are inconsiderately persistent.”</p>
<p class="continue"><<link "Continue through the swamp." "SwampCapture">><</link>></p>

:: SwampCapture [art-12]
<p class="narration">They emerged scratched and exhausted, directly in front of Humperdinck and his armed men.</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Humperdinck:</span> “You have led me on an unpleasant chase.”</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Buttercup:</span> “We were hoping you'd stop.”</p>
<p class="narration">Westley was seized. Buttercup was taken back to the palace.</p>
<p class="continue"><<link "Continue to the castle outskirts." "MachineOpening">><</link>></p>

:: MachineOpening [art-13]
<p class="narration">Within the castle, Count Rugen oversaw a machine built to cause suffering. Westley was its prisoner. By the time Fezzik found news of him, the man in black was barely alive.</p>
<p class="narration">Iñigo had searched for Rugen for years. The knowledge that the count was close made his hands shake, but it did not make his next decision easier.</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Fezzik:</span> “We need to help our friend.”</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Iñigo:</span> “He defeated me. I have been trying to decide whether that makes us friends.”</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Fezzik:</span> “He didn't kill you.”</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Iñigo:</span> “A persuasive argument.”</p>
<p>Iñigo proposes a rescue plan.</p>
<ul class="choices">
	<li><<link "“We storm the gates.”" "MachineStorm">><</link>></li>
	<li><<link "“We find someone who can save a dying man.”" "MachineHealer">><</link>></li>
	<li><<link "“We disguise ourselves as guards.”" "MachineDisguise">><</link>></li>
</ul>

:: MachineStorm [art-13]
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Fezzik:</span> “I could throw you over the wall.”</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Iñigo:</span> “And then?”</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Fezzik:</span> “I haven't planned the landing.”</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Iñigo:</span> “We shall keep thinking.”</p>
<p class="continue"><<link "Try another plan." "MachineOpening">><</link>></p>

:: MachineHealer [art-13]
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Fezzik:</span> “I know a healer who argues with patients about whether they're alive.”</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Iñigo:</span> “A professional optimist?”</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Fezzik:</span> “More of a professional arguer.”</p>
<p class="narration">They carried Westley towards a cottage outside town. Iñigo's revenge would have to wait. Saving a friend could not.</p>
<p class="continue"><<link "Visit Miracle Max." "MaxConsultation">><</link>></p>

:: MachineDisguise [art-13]
<p class="narration">Fezzik holds a guard's jacket against his chest. It covers one shoulder.</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Fezzik:</span> “Maybe if I don't breathe.”</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Iñigo:</span> “I'd prefer you did.”</p>
<p class="continue"><<link "Try another plan." "MachineOpening">><</link>></p>

:: MaxConsultation [art-14]
<p class="narration">Miracle Max opened the door, saw Westley, and tried to close it again.</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Max:</span> “Retired.”</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Valerie (inside):</span> “You said that yesterday.”</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Max:</span> “Yesterday I was younger.”</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Fezzik:</span> “Our friend needs help.”</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Max:</span> “Most people do. It's why I retired.”</p>
<p class="narration">Valerie pushed past him and looked at Westley.</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Valerie:</span> “Bring him in.”</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Max:</span> “We have not discussed the fee!”</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Valerie:</span> “We have not discussed whether you're going to be useful.”</p>
<p>Fezzik tries to persuade Max.</p>
<ul class="choices">
	<li><<link "Appeal to compassion." "MaxCompassion">><</link>></li>
	<li><<link "Mention Humperdinck." "MaxHumperdinck">><</link>></li>
	<li><<link "Offer everything in Fezzik's pockets." "MaxPockets">><</link>></li>
</ul>

:: MaxCompassion [art-14]
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Fezzik:</span> “He's our friend.”</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Max:</span> “A terrible argument. Friends are notoriously difficult to invoice.”</p>
<p class="narration">Valerie brings a blanket.</p>
<p class="continue"><<link "Continue." "MaxExam">><</link>></p>

:: MaxHumperdinck [art-14]
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Fezzik:</span> “The prince did this.”</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Max:</span> “That peacock? Why didn't you begin with the diagnosis?”</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Valerie:</span> “Because that's not a diagnosis.”</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Max:</span> “It is in this house.”</p>
<p class="continue"><<link "Continue." "MaxExam">><</link>></p>

:: MaxPockets [art-14]
<p class="narration">He produces a button, a stone and some string. Max inspects the stone.</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Max:</span> “Excellent stone. The rest is offensive.”</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Fezzik:</span> “I can take the string back.”</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Max:</span> “Don't be hasty.”</p>
<p class="continue"><<link "Continue." "MaxExam">><</link>></p>

:: MaxExam [art-14]
<p class="narration">Max examined Westley, frowned, examined him again, and announced three incompatible conclusions.</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Iñigo:</span> “Can you save him?”</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Max:</span> “That depends on whether he intends to cooperate.”</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Valerie:</span> “He's unconscious.”</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Max:</span> “An unpromising start.”</p>
<p>What should Fezzik do while Max works?</p>
<ul class="choices">
	<li><<link "Ask for a medical explanation." "MaxExplanation">><</link>></li>
	<li><<link "Hold Westley's hand." "MaxHand">><</link>></li>
	<li><<link "Suggest a second opinion." "MaxOpinion">><</link>></li>
</ul>

:: MaxExplanation [art-14]
<p class="narration">Max gives one so long and contradictory that Valerie interrupts to translate: “He's trying.”</p>
<p class="continue"><<link "Continue." "MaxRejoin">><</link>></p>

:: MaxHand [art-14]
<p class="narration">Fezzik does, carefully.</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Max:</span> “Good. If he wakes up frightened, tell him I'm the competent one.”</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Valerie:</span> “Don't lie to the patient.”</p>
<p class="continue"><<link "Continue." "MaxRejoin">><</link>></p>

:: MaxOpinion [art-14]
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Max:</span> “Valerie!”</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Valerie:</span> “I agree with the giant.”</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Max:</span> “I withdraw my request.”</p>
<p class="continue"><<link "Continue." "MaxRejoin">><</link>></p>

:: MaxRejoin [art-14]
<p class="narration">At last Westley opened his eyes. His body was far less enthusiastic about the development.</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Westley:</span> “Did it work?”</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Max:</span> “You are speaking.”</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Westley:</span> “Is that a yes?”</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Valerie:</span> “It's the closest you're going to get.”</p>
<p class="dialogue framing-dialogue"><span class="speaker">Grandson:</span> “Is Max a real doctor?”</p>
<p class="dialogue framing-dialogue"><span class="speaker">Grandfather:</span> “He has an excellent bedside manner, provided the bed is somewhere else.”</p>
<p class="dialogue framing-dialogue"><span class="speaker">Grandson:</span> “So no?”</p>
<p class="dialogue framing-dialogue"><span class="speaker">Grandfather:</span> “So let's be grateful Valerie was there.”</p>
<p class="narration">Westley could speak and think, but barely move. That was enough for his friends to begin planning something spectacularly foolish.</p>
<p class="continue"><<link "Plan the rescue." "CastleAssault">><</link>></p>

:: CastleAssault [art-15]
<p class="narration">The castle had high walls, armed guards and a wedding underway. The rescue party consisted of one giant, one swordsman and one man who could barely sit upright.</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Iñigo:</span> “We need an army.”</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Westley:</span> “We have Fezzik.”</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Fezzik:</span> “I am not an army.”</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Westley:</span> “Try not to disappoint us.”</p>
<p>How do they frighten the guards?</p>
<ul class="choices">
	<li><<link "Create a monstrous silhouette." "CastleSilhouette">><</link>></li>
	<li><<link "Challenge the captain to a duel." "CastleDuel">><</link>></li>
	<li><<link "Pretend to be two enormous armies." "CastleArmies">><</link>></li>
</ul>

:: CastleSilhouette [art-15]
<p class="narration">Fezzik raises a cloaked figure above the gate while Westley supplies an ominous warning. The guards scatter.</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Fezzik:</span> “I think I frightened them.”</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Iñigo:</span> “You frightened me, and I knew it was you.”</p>
<p class="continue"><<link "Enter the castle." "CastleGateOpen">><</link>></p>

:: CastleDuel [art-15]
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Captain:</span> “Archers!”</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Iñigo:</span> “I was hoping for a more intimate contest.”</p>
<p class="narration">Arrows strike the ground nearby.</p>
<p class="continue"><<link "Try another approach." "CastleAssault">><</link>></p>

:: CastleArmies [art-15]
<p class="narration">Fezzik shouts both sides of an imaginary argument.</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Guard:</span> “Why do they all sound like one man?”</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Westley:</span> “An excellent question. Retreat.”</p>
<p class="continue"><<link "Try another approach." "CastleAssault">><</link>></p>

:: CastleGateOpen [art-15]
<p class="dialogue framing-dialogue"><span class="speaker">Grandson:</span> “They're attacking a castle with three people?”</p>
<p class="dialogue framing-dialogue"><span class="speaker">Grandfather:</span> “Technically two and a half. One can barely stand.”</p>
<p class="dialogue framing-dialogue"><span class="speaker">Grandson:</span> “That's a terrible plan.”</p>
<p class="dialogue framing-dialogue"><span class="speaker">Grandfather:</span> “Yes. Fortunately, it's also a very loud one.”</p>
<p class="narration">The guards fled the gate. Iñigo and Fezzik carried Westley inside before anyone could reconsider.</p>
<p class="continue"><<link "Continue through the castle." "RugenOpening">><</link>></p>

:: RugenOpening [art-16]
<p class="narration">Iñigo found Count Rugen in a corridor lined with tapestries. The count recognised him too late to pretend otherwise.</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Rugen:</span> “You are making a serious mistake.”</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Iñigo:</span> “I've had years to consider it.”</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Rugen:</span> “I can pay you.”</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Iñigo:</span> “You have misunderstood the debt.”</p>
<p>How does Iñigo answer Rugen's attempt to escape responsibility?</p>
<ul class="choices">
	<li><<link "“You cannot bargain away what you did.”" "RugenBargain">><</link>></li>
	<li><<link "“For once, stop talking.”" "RugenSilence">><</link>></li>
	<li><<link "“You should have remembered my father.”" "RugenFather">><</link>></li>
</ul>

:: RugenBargain [art-16]
<p class="narration">Rugen's smile falters. He reaches for his weapon.</p>
<p class="continue"><<link "Continue." "RugenRejoin">><</link>></p>

:: RugenSilence [art-16]
<p class="narration">Rugen takes a breath to object. Iñigo draws his sword.</p>
<p class="continue"><<link "Continue." "RugenRejoin">><</link>></p>

:: RugenFather [art-16]
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Rugen:</span> “I remember many men.”</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Iñigo:</span> “Then remember this one.”</p>
<p class="continue"><<link "Continue." "RugenRejoin">><</link>></p>

:: RugenRejoin [art-16]
<p class="narration">Their duel was brutal. Rugen fought to survive; Iñigo fought for the father he had lost. At last Rugen fell.</p>
<p class="narration">Iñigo stood still. He had imagined this moment for years. It did not return a single lost day.</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Iñigo:</span> “I thought it would feel different.”</p>
<p class="narration">No one answered. For a moment, the castle was quiet.</p>
<p class="continue"><<link "Find Buttercup." "PrinceOpening">><</link>></p>

:: PrinceOpening [art-17]
<p class="narration">Humperdinck entered Buttercup's chamber with the satisfied air of a man expecting applause.</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Humperdinck:</span> “Everything is under control.”</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Buttercup:</span> “You keep saying that. Is it a royal motto?”</p>
<p class="narration">The door opened again. Westley stood in the doorway, pale and unsteady, supporting himself against the frame.</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Humperdinck:</span> “You!”</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Westley:</span> “I'm told that is my name.”</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Humperdinck:</span> “Guards!”</p>
<p class="narration">No one came.</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Buttercup:</span> “Perhaps they've found better employment.”</p>
<p>How does Buttercup seize the moment?</p>
<ul class="choices">
	<li><<link "Stand beside Westley." "PrinceStand">><</link>></li>
	<li><<link "Demand that the prince explain himself." "PrinceDemand">><</link>></li>
	<li><<link "Pretend to obey." "PrincePretend">><</link>></li>
</ul>

:: PrinceStand [art-17]
<p class="narration">She crosses the room.</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Humperdinck:</span> “You cannot simply ignore my orders!”</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Buttercup:</span> “I've been practising.”</p>
<p class="continue"><<link "Continue." "PrinceRejoin">><</link>></p>

:: PrinceDemand [art-17]
<p class="narration">Humperdinck launches into a speech about duty and the realm.</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Buttercup:</span> “Can you give us the version without yourself in it?”</p>
<p class="narration">He cannot.</p>
<p class="continue"><<link "Continue." "PrinceRejoin">><</link>></p>

:: PrincePretend [art-17]
<p class="narration">She steps towards the prince and slides his sword beyond his reach.</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Westley:</span> “A convincing performance.”</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Buttercup:</span> “I learned from an expert.”</p>
<p class="continue"><<link "Continue." "PrinceRejoin">><</link>></p>

:: PrinceRejoin [art-17]
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Humperdinck:</span> “You cannot defeat me!”</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Westley:</span> “Then it must be terribly embarrassing that you already look defeated.”</p>
<p class="narration">Humperdinck looked at Buttercup, the empty doorway and the sword he could no longer reach. He chose not to test his courage.</p>
<p class="continue"><<link "Leave the castle." "EscapeOpening">><</link>></p>

:: EscapeOpening [art-18]
<p class="narration">Iñigo and Fezzik arrived in time to find Westley leaning against the wall.</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Fezzik:</span> “Can you walk?”</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Westley:</span> “In theory.”</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Iñigo:</span> “I suggest we test that theory outside the castle.”</p>
<p>What does Buttercup say as they leave?</p>
<ul class="choices">
	<li><<link "“Has anyone remembered the horses?”" "EscapeHorses">><</link>></li>
	<li><<link "“Do we have a plan for the guards?”" "EscapeGuards">><</link>></li>
	<li><<link "“No one is going back for the prince.”" "EscapePrince">><</link>></li>
</ul>

:: EscapeHorses [art-18]
<p class="narration">Fezzik smiles.</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Fezzik:</span> “I remembered four.”</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Westley:</span> “Then you are officially in charge of practical matters.”</p>
<p class="continue"><<link "Ride out." "EscapeRejoin">><</link>></p>

:: EscapeGuards [art-18]
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Iñigo:</span> “Run.”</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Buttercup:</span> “That's your plan?”</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Iñigo:</span> “It's shorter than our previous ones.”</p>
<p class="continue"><<link "Ride out." "EscapeRejoin">><</link>></p>

:: EscapePrince [art-18]
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Westley:</span> “I was going to suggest a farewell speech.”</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Buttercup:</span> “Don't.”</p>
<p class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">Westley:</span> “A wise correction.”</p>
<p class="continue"><<link "Ride out." "EscapeRejoin">><</link>></p>

:: EscapeRejoin [art-18]
<p class="narration">They rode into the night, four friends escaping a castle that had never expected anyone to argue with its prince and win.</p>
<p class="narration">Back in the bedroom, the grandson leaned forward.</p>
<p class="continue"><<link "Turn to the last page." "LastPageOpening">><</link>></p>

:: LastPageOpening [art-01]
<p class="narration">The grandfather closed the book. Outside, the rain had stopped.</p>
<p class="dialogue framing-dialogue"><span class="speaker">Grandson:</span> “So the giant was kind, the swordsman was brave, and the prince was an idiot.”</p>
<p class="dialogue framing-dialogue"><span class="speaker">Grandfather:</span> “A concise and largely accurate summary.”</p>
<p class="dialogue framing-dialogue"><span class="speaker">Grandson:</span> “And the lovers got away.”</p>
<p class="dialogue framing-dialogue"><span class="speaker">Grandfather:</span> “They did.”</p>
<p class="dialogue framing-dialogue"><span class="speaker">Grandson:</span> “There was quite a lot of kissing for a sword-fighting story.”</p>
<p class="dialogue framing-dialogue"><span class="speaker">Grandfather:</span> “There was quite a lot of sword fighting for a kissing story.”</p>
<p>What does the boy ask before his grandfather leaves?</p>
<ul class="choices">
	<li><<link "“Could you read it again?”" "LastPageAgain">><</link>></li>
	<li><<link "“Next time, more sword fights?”" "LastPageSwords">><</link>></li>
	<li><<link "“What happened to Iñigo afterwards?”" "LastPageInigo">><</link>></li>
</ul>

:: LastPageAgain [art-01]
<p class="dialogue framing-dialogue"><span class="speaker">Grandfather:</span> “Of course.”</p>
<p class="dialogue framing-dialogue"><span class="speaker">Grandson:</span> “Tomorrow. I need to recover from the romance.”</p>
<p class="continue"><<link "Close the book." "LastPageEnding">><</link>></p>

:: LastPageSwords [art-01]
<p class="dialogue framing-dialogue"><span class="speaker">Grandfather:</span> “I'll consult the swordsmen.”</p>
<p class="dialogue framing-dialogue"><span class="speaker">Grandson:</span> “And fewer speeches from the prince.”</p>
<p class="dialogue framing-dialogue"><span class="speaker">Grandfather:</span> “A request shared by the entire kingdom.”</p>
<p class="continue"><<link "Close the book." "LastPageEnding">><</link>></p>

:: LastPageInigo [art-01]
<p class="dialogue framing-dialogue"><span class="speaker">Grandfather:</span> “He had to discover who he was without a revenge to pursue.”</p>
<p class="dialogue framing-dialogue"><span class="speaker">Grandson:</span> “Does that story have swords?”</p>
<p class="dialogue framing-dialogue"><span class="speaker">Grandfather:</span> “Almost certainly.”</p>
<p class="continue"><<link "Close the book." "LastPageEnding">><</link>></p>

:: LastPageEnding [art-18]
<p class="narration">The grandfather placed the book on the bedside table. The boy glanced at it once more before turning out the light.</p>
<p class="narration">On the final page, four riders disappeared into the moonlit distance.</p>
<p class="narration"><strong>THE END</strong></p>
